Release Notes unified i.MX6 Linux BSP:
======================================

BSP-Yocto-i.MX6-PD16.1.1                2018-02-07
==================================================
- Linux Kernel v4.1.46 (v4.1 is a LTS kernel)
  * Update from v4.1.36 to v4.1.46
- barebox v2016.11.0
- Yocto 2.1.3 (krogoth)
- Qt 5.6.3 from meta-qt5 (krogoth)

Tested Yocto Images:
--------------------
- phytec-qt5demo-image

Build Environment:
------------------
- Ubuntu 14.04 64Bit


Changes since PD16.1.0:
-----------------------
- New Features:
  * Added support for ISSI and Winbond NOR flash
    - Winbond W25Q128
    - ISSI IS25LP128
  * Added support for Winbond NAND

- Fixes:
  * barebox:
    - Barebox devicetree now supports environment on SPI-NOR flash.
    - Fixed the CS0_END RAM setting for the i.MX 6QuadPlus.
    - Fixed a bug described by erratum ERR007117 which led to an infrequent
      detection failure of the NAND flash during boot.
    - Improved RAM timings for i.MX6 DualLite\Solo (400 MHz) on all phyFLEX
      machines.

  * kernel:
    - CAN is now working with 10 kbaud.
    - A bug was fixed where the LVDS display sometimes did not show anything
      after boot. This bug is described in erratum ERR009219.
    - Fixed a typo in the HDMI devicetree node which prevented DDC to work
      correctly.
    - The npwrdn GPIO assignement on the phytec-mediabus was fixed from GPIO5_27
      to GPIO3_9 on the phyBOARD-Mira.
    - Fixed a bug described by erratum ERR007117 which led to an infrequent
      detection failure of the NAND flash during boot.
    - Fixed a GPU stability issue where the GPU clocks run on clock rates which
      were to high by default.
    - Fixed a stability issue when switching the internal LDOs of the
      i.MX 6DualLight into bypass mode.
    - Introduced small performance improvements by disabling spinlock debug
      logging which is enabled by default.


Known Issues:
-------------
- Display and HDMI do not work with the QuadPlus
- The LDB_DI0_SEL and LDB_DI1_SEL mux can only be set in the devicetree and
  cannot be changed on runtime


BSP-Yocto-i.MX6-PD16.1.0                2017-01-23
==================================================
Features:
-------------
- barebox/yocto: env refactoring in barebox-env in meta-phytec
- barebox: nv variables are saved automatically on shutdown
- implemenet DA9062 and DA9063 Watchdog and reboot handler for phyFLEX and phyCORE
  in kernel and barebox watchdog is not enable by default
- Enable double buffering in i.MX6 OpenGL Library and Qt
- update vivante GPU library for i.MX6 QuadPLus
- VM-012 support (vita1300)
- RS485 Support
- gstreamer: add kmssink
- gstreamer: add v4l2 encoder for i.MX6 VPU
- gstreamer: add bayer2rgb-neon
- tuxracer recipe in meta-yogurt
- bvtest: crop support

Fixed Issues:
-------------
- Fix: i.MX6 DualLite/Solo Stability Issue at 396 Mhz.
    Linux kernel patch "ARM: dts: imx6dl: Fix the VDD_ARM_CAP voltage for 396MHz operation".
    Fixes Phytec's LPN-226e_1.
- fix phyCORE-i.MX6 stability (PMIC buckets)
- linux-mainline: fix Micrel ethernet phy link detection issues at -30°C
- linux-mainline: fix VM-010-BW and VM-010-COL for phyBOARD-SUBRA

Notes:
------
Updating the kernel, device tree and rootfs has changed in BSP-Yocto-i.MX6-PD16.1.0. As kernel and device tree are now placed
in a static ubi volume inside the rootfs partition.
Following example shows how to update those parts in NAND from Network with the new barebox loaded:

 bootloader$ ubiformat -y /dev/nand0.root
 bootloader$ ubiattach /dev/nand0.root

 bootloader$ ubimkvol -t static /dev/nand0.root.ubi kernel 8M
 bootloader$ ubimkvol -t static /dev/nand0.root.ubi oftree 1M
 bootloader$ ubimkvol -t dynamic /dev/nand0.root.ubi root 0

 bootloader$ ubiupdatevol /dev/nand0.root.ubi.kernel /mnt/tftp/linuximage
 bootloader$ ubiupdatevol /dev/nand0.root.ubi.oftree /mnt/tftp/oftree
 bootloader$ cp /mnt/tftp/rootfs.ubifs /dev/nand0.root.ubi.root
